    "note": "Single-feature spec (feature 13, long), found on the very first move (init, best of 80 candidates) with no further search or iteration. In-sample Sharpe 1.627 net of costs. Minimal search here reduces overfitting risk relative to a multi-move search, but init itself already picks the best of 80 candidates in-sample, so some optimism bias remains. I expect substantial shrinkage OOS -- typical for daily equity/futures style signals net of realistic costs -- landing around 0.6-0.9 Sharpe, with real uncertainty given it's a single feature (no diversification benefit across features) and the possibility the signal is partly a regime-specific artifact."
